Task: Tour wrapper module (source/tours/)

Summary: Added driver.js 1.3.6 (pinned, MIT) as the tour engine and a thin
declarative wrapper, source/tours/engine.js. Tours are defined as step lists
({element?, title, description}); resolveSteps() drops steps whose anchor is
absent from the DOM (so one definition serves screens in different states),
element-less steps become centered modal steps. createTour() builds a driver
instance with progress UI, animation disabled under prefers-reduced-motion,
and onDestroyed wired to the caller's onFinish (finish and dismiss both count
as seen). startTour() creates+drives and reports whether anything was shown.

Files:
- source/tours/engine.js (new)
- tests/js/tours/engine.test.js (new, 11 tests — TDD red confirmed first)
- package.json / package-lock.json (driver.js 1.3.6 exact)

Why: FR-1 of the onboarding-tours spec — a free (MIT) intro.js-style engine
behind a declarative API so later tour definitions need no driver.js
knowledge.
